Q: MongoDB Atlas Search Index Query Required A: <ul>
<li>Case: <code>searchOn = &quot;all&quot;</code></li>
</ul>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>{
  $search: {
    index: &quot;your_index_name&quot;,
    compound: {
      should: [
        { autocomplete: { query: searchTerm, path: &quot;firstName&quot; } },
        { autocomplete: { query: searchTerm, path: &quot;lastName&quot; } },
        { autocomplete: { query: searchTerm, path: &quot;email&quot; } }
      ],
      minimumShouldMatch: 1
    }
  }
}
</code></pre>
<ul>
<li>Case: <code>searchOn = &quot;firstName&quot;</code> / <code>&quot;lastName&quot;</code> / <code>&quot;email&quot;</code></li>
</ul>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>{
  $search: {
    index: &quot;your_index_name&quot;,
    autocomplete: {
      query: searchTerm,
      path: searchOn
    }
  }
}
</code></pre>
<p>I recommend you like following:</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>const buildSearchStage = (searchTerm, searchOn) =&gt; {
  if (searchOn === &quot;all&quot;) {
    return {
      $search: {
        index: &quot;your_index_name&quot;,
        compound: {
          should: [
            { autocomplete: { query: searchTerm, path: &quot;firstName&quot; } },
            { autocomplete: { query: searchTerm, path: &quot;lastName&quot; } },
            { autocomplete: { query: searchTerm, path: &quot;email&quot; } }
          ],
          minimumShouldMatch: 1
        }
      }
    };
  }

  return {
    $search: {
      index: &quot;your_index_name&quot;,
      autocomplete: {
        query: searchTerm,
        path: searchOn
      }
    }
  };
};
</code></pre>
<p>This covers all your case cleanly.</p>

Q: Sky not Painting A: <p>(I have corrected to the conventional spelling.)</p>
<p>Though AmericanFlag is a Painter, from any Painter you cannot call PaintSky.</p>
<pre><code>AmericanFlag painter = new AmericanFlag();
painter.paintSky();
</code></pre>
<p>And the PaintSky method should use boolean different. <code>= true</code> is an assignment, not equality <code>==</code>. And booleans are immediately true/false values. Note that <code>! X</code> means <strong>not</strong> X.</p>
<p>I did not correct any logic errors, that is your home work. Where <code>||</code> means <strong>or</strong> and <code>&amp;&amp;</code> means <strong>and</strong>.</p>
<pre><code>public void paintSky() {
    for (int x = 0; x &lt; 31; x++){
        if (isFacingEast() || canMove()) {
            movePaint();
        } else if (!canMove()) {
            turnRight();
            move();
            turnRight();
        } else if (isFacingWest() || canMove()) {
            movePaint();
        } else {
            turnLeft();
            move();
            turnLeft();
        }
    }
}
</code></pre>
